# CODEOWNERS — mirrors the ownership table in CLAUDE.md ("System Boundaries").
#
# All entries currently resolve to the repo owner handle; the comments record
# which TEAM owns each boundary so review routing can be split into real
# GitHub teams later without re-deriving the map.
#
# Later rules win over earlier ones for overlapping paths.

# Root config + CI/CD + tooling → platform team (Team A)
*                                   @mosnin
/scripts/                           @mosnin
/.github/                           @mosnin

# apps/web (UI, API routes, Clerk integration) → web team
/apps/web/                          @mosnin

# convex/ (schema, queries, mutations, auth config) → data team
/convex/                            @mosnin

# packages/ (contracts + sdk + cli) → sdk team (contracts types reviewed with data team)
/packages/                          @mosnin

# packages/mcp (read-only MCP server over the /api/v1 read API) → platform team (Team A)
# Read surface only: no write tools, no direct convex/ imports. See docs/mcp.md.
/packages/mcp/                      @mosnin

# Shared docs and tests — any team may edit; platform reviews structure
/docs/                              @mosnin
/tests/                             @mosnin
